\pard\sl-240\slmult1 \cf1\lang1033\fs24\f0 Alice's Restaurant Anti-Massacree Adventure\par
\cf2 Thanksgiving 1965.  You are 19 years old.  Since getting booted out of college due to a lack of interest and a corresponding lack of grade points you have been playing music in coffee houses for tips.  You're not sure exactly what you want to do with your life now.  You'd like to make a living playing music, if you could only write a hit song.  But what are the odds of that?  One thing you know for sure, you don't want to go to Vietnam.  Now that you're not a student, they'll be wanting you to go.  With your long hair and a guitar slung over your shoulder, you're hardly the military type.  You're looking forward to spending Thanksgiving with your friend Alice and putting all of this out of your mind.  Alice lives in an old church building and she makes a Thanksgiving dinner that can't be beat.  You have pulled your red VW Microbus up to the side of the building and you are now standing in front of the church.\par
\cf1 \par
open mailbox\par
\cf2 The mailbox is open.  When you open the mailbox an envelope falls out and lands at your feet.\par
\cf1 \par
take envelope\par
\cf2 You have the envelope.\par
\cf1 \par
open envelope\par
\cf2 Opening the envelope reveals a letter.\par
\cf1 \par
read letter\par
\cf2 The letter informs you that you are to report to Whitehall Street in New York for your army physical a week from today.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are at a wooden gothic arched doorway.   You can move east, south and out.\par
\cf1 \par
knock on church door\par
\cf2 Knock.  Knock.    The door opens and reveals Alice.  She immediately hugs you and welcomes you inside.  She apologizes for the mess.  Having all this room where the pews used to be, she hasn't taken out her garbage for a very long time.  It is piled up in a corner of the otherwise very nice sanctuary.  She updates you with stories of your mutual friends and about how the construction on the inside of the church is coming along.  Facha also seems happy to see you.  The dog runs in circles and wags its tail.  Alice laughs and tells you that Facha has been quite a naughty dog lately.  She has gotten into the habit of digging in the garden.  She thinks that the dog has even been burying odd things in the yard.  Alice gestures towards a table set with a Thanksgiving dinner that couldn't be beat.  There is stuffing, cranberry sauce, and an impressive turkey.  \par
\cf1 \par
sit\par
\cf2 You are now seated.\par
\cf1 \par
eat turkey\par
\cf2 As you enjoy the Thanksgiving Dinner That Couldn't Be Beat, Alice tells you that she has opened a restaurant.  "A restaurant?" you say.  "Not just any restaurant," she says.  "This is a special restaurant.  There will be no square meals there.  You should go see it later.  It's just a half a mile from the railroad track."  "Far out," you say, and finish your feast leaving only a large turkey bone on your plate.\par
\cf1 \par
take bone\par
\cf2 You pick up the bone.\par
\cf1 \par
give dog bone\par
\cf2 With a delighted bark, the dog grabs the bone and heads outside.  "You've made her day," says Alice.  "There she goes to dig in my yard again."  In a few moments, Facha returns, tracking in a fair ammount of dirt.\par
\cf1 \par
south\par
\cf2 You move south.\par
You are in front of a gothic wooden church.  The paint is peeling and the stained glass windows are in disrepair, but it retains much of its beauty and charm especially at this time of year.   Although the colors reached their peak a couple of weeks ago there are still enough orange leaves on the trees to remind you of a New England post card.  On the east side of the church you can make out Alice's garden.  Your VW microbus is parked here on a road heading north.  You'll have to get back in the bus if you want to go that way.  It's too far to walk.  There is a mailbox here.  You can move north and east.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
You are in Alice's garden.   Although the growing season has largely passed there are still some flowers and vegetables here.  The sunflowers seem to have toppled.  You are in Alice's garden.   The dog appears to have been busy.    There are several new holes in the ground and roots and bulbs have been brought to the surface along with some blue rocks.  These are slag from the old iron furnace that once supported the workers of the town.  They must have been buried for years.    Also here is an implement of destruction.  You can move north and west.\par
\cf1 \par
take implement of destruction\par
\cf2 You pick up an implement of destruction.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are at the stable.  Back in the days when this was an active church, it had room for 10 horses.  The stalls smell distinctly of manure and straw.   In the back of the stable there is an old cabinet of some kind.  Horse is here.  You can only move south.\par
\cf1 \par
play guitar\par
\cf2  Maybe it's just your imagination, but it seems like the horse is listening.  It has stopped eating for the moment and is swaying its head in time to the music.\par
\cf1 \par
south\par
\cf2 You move south.\par
You are in Alice's garden.   Although the growing season has largely passed there are still some flowers and vegetables here.  The sunflowers seem to have toppled.  You are in Alice's garden.   The dog appears to have been busy.    There are several new holes in the ground and roots and bulbs have been brought to the surface along with some blue rocks.  These are slag from the old iron furnace that once supported the workers of the town.  They must have been buried for years.    You can move north and west.  Horse walks towards you from the north.\par
\cf1 \par
stop playing\par
\cf2 Ok, you're not playing any more.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are at the stable.  Back in the days when this was an active church, it had room for 10 horses.  The stalls smell distinctly of manure and straw.   In the back of the stable there is an old cabinet of some kind.  You can only move south.\par
\cf1 \par
open cabinet\par
\cf2 The cabinet opens and a shovel falls out, nearly bonking you on the head.\par
\cf1 \par
take shovel\par
\cf2 You have the shovel.\par
\cf1 \par
south\par
\cf2 You move south.\par
You are in Alice's garden.   Although the growing season has largely passed there are still some flowers and vegetables here.  The sunflowers seem to have toppled.  You are in Alice's garden.   The dog appears to have been busy.    There are several new holes in the ground and roots and bulbs have been brought to the surface along with some blue rocks.  These are slag from the old iron furnace that once supported the workers of the town.  They must have been buried for years.    Horse is here.  You can move north and west.\par
\cf1 \par
west\par
\cf2 You move west.\par
You are in front of a gothic wooden church.  The paint is peeling and the stained glass windows are in disrepair, but it retains much of its beauty and charm especially at this time of year.   Although the colors reached their peak a couple of weeks ago there are still enough orange leaves on the trees to remind you of a New England post card.  On the east side of the church you can make out Alice's garden.  Your VW microbus is parked here on a road heading north.  You'll have to get back in the bus if you want to go that way.  It's too far to walk.  There is a mailbox here.  You can move north and east.\par
\cf1 \par
get in bus\par
\cf2 You are behind the wheel of the red VW microbus.  To steer, type "drive" and the direction you would like to go.\par
\cf1 \par
drive north\par
\cf2 You drive north.  You are in front of the Town Dump.  There are roads leading northeast, east and south.   You can not continue to the dump itself because there is a fence and a chain across the road with a sign on it that you can't quite make out from the driver's seat of the Red VW microbus. \par
\cf1 \par
get out of bus\par
\cf2 You're now on foot.\par
\cf1 \par
take sign\par
\cf2 You have stolen the sign that says "Closed on Thanksgiving."  Don't let Officer Obie catch you.\par
\cf1 \par
get in bus\par
\cf2 You're in the red VW microbus.\par
\cf1 \par
drive east\par
\cf2 You drive east.  You are in the red VW microbus in the parking area near Alice's Restaurant.  There is a sidewalk heading to the restaurant.  The road goes to the west from here.\par
\cf1 \par
get out of bus\par
\cf2 You are on foot.  This is the front of Alice's famous restaurant.  It looks like a hole-in-the-wall but you're sure the inside must have a few homey touches.   Your red VW microbus is parked nearby.   As you step towards the door, a rude man blocks your path.  "Where do you think you're going you long haired hippie perversion?"  he asks.    Rude Customer is here.\par
\cf1 \par
put sign on window\par
\cf2 The rude man looks at the sign and slowly reads "closed on Thanksgiving."  He seems to be processing the information.  "Oh, it's closed," he says finally.  The man shrugs and goes home.  Rude Customer walks off.\par
\cf1 \par
open restaurant door\par
\cf2 The door is open.\par
\cf1 \par
in\par
\cf2 You move in.\par
It looks like your basic diner except for a few homey decorations over the grill.   There are booths and a counter.  On the counter is a tray.  Also here is a brownie.  You can only move out.\par
\cf1 \par
take brownie\par
\cf2 You pick up the brownie.\par
\cf1 \par
out\par
\cf2 You move out.\par
This is the front of Alice's famous restaurant.  It looks like a hole-in-the-wall but you're sure the inside must have a few homey touches.   Your red VW microbus is parked nearby.  Also here is a sign.  You can only move in.\par
\cf1 \par
get in bus\par
\cf2 You hop in.  You are in the red VW microbus in the parking area near Alice's Restaurant.  There is a sidewalk heading to the restaurant.  The road goes to the west from here.\par
\cf1 \par
drive west\par
\cf2 You drive west.  You are in front of the Town Dump.  There are roads leading northeast, east and south.  The dump is closed on Thanksgiving.\par
\cf1 \par
drive south\par
\cf2 You drive south.  You are in your red VW microbus which is parked in front of the church.  The road leads to the north from here.  \par
\cf1 \par
get out of bus\par
\cf2 You're on foot.  You are in front of a gothic wooden church.  The paint is peeling and the stained glass windows are in disrepair, but it retains much of its beauty and charm especially at this time of year.   Although the colors reached their peak a couple of weeks ago there are still enough orange leaves on the trees to remind you of a New England post card.  On the east side of the church you can make out Alice's garden.  Your VW microbus is parked here on a road heading north.  You'll have to get back in the bus if you want to go that way.  It's too far to walk.  There is a mailbox here.  You are no longer in the bus.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are at a wooden gothic arched doorway.   You can move north, east, south, in and out.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
The sanctuary has a high arched roof.  A few of the stained glass windows have been broken, but most are still intact.  They are mostly light blue and depict religious scenes, chalices and lillies.  Above the door is the impressive rose window which has images of Matthew, Mark, Luke and John.  At the northern end of the sanctuary is the area that once held the altar.  The attractiveness of the room is marred somewhat by the presence of a large pile of garbage in the corner.   To the west is the bell tower.   Alice and Facha are here.  You can move south, west and out.\par
\cf1 \par
eat brownie\par
\cf2 The brownie has a rich chocolate flavor.  Your thought that this may be the best brownie you ever tasted is interrupted by another thought... or is it a feeling.  Yes, it is more like a feeling.  You feel... light.  You are sure you have powers.  You are pretty sure that you can walk right through the wall.  Something tells you not to try that though.  Instead you start to float.  You are up near the ceiling looking down.  You notice a lot of dust on top of things.  You start to think about the nature of dust.  Isn't dust really the essence of life itself?  I mean,  I mean... Wow, you're really floating.  You turn a back flip or two... You feel so peaceful just floating... Some time passes and you wonder... Does it make sense that I can fly?  You start to come down.  You sit in one of the booths for a while before things seem pretty much normal again.  You decide to save the other half the brownie for another occasion.\par
\cf1 \par
west\par
\cf2 You move west.\par
You are below the bell tower.  As you look up you can see the floor of a small room above, but where there ought to be stairs or a ladder there is nothing.  Apparently they haven't got done building that part yet.  You can only move east.\par
\cf1 \par
eat half brownie\par
\cf2 You feel yourself swirling up among colorful sparkles.  Chicken flying everywhere around the bell tower.  You're going up and up.  You think you know what it is like to be a leaf in the fall.  Oh, no, except leaves fall down and you're floating up.  Well, sometimes leave float up, when there's an updraft or something.  The leaf floats up and then it drifts back and forth on the breeze and gently lands as you are now on the floor of the bell tower.  You are in a small room that has been built in the old bell tower.  The bell is still here above your head.  There is a tiny square window cut into the wall in the middle of a round embellishment on the facade.  The room is stuffy and dusty.  It has obviously not been used for some time.  There is a variety of junk stored up here.  Also here is a rake.\par
\cf1 \par
take rake\par
\cf2 You pick up the rake.\par
\cf1 \par
call for help\par
\cf2 You shout but Alice doesn't seem to hear you.\par
\cf1 \par
ring bell\par
\cf2 You pull the cord and the heavy bell swings from side to side.  The weight of it nearly pulls you over.  You're afraid it might come crashing down on you.  After two rings though you hear a voice from below.  It's Alice.  "Is someone ringing the bell?!"  You go to the hole where the stairs used to be and look down.  Alice is looking up at you.  "What are you doing up there?" she asks.  "How did you get there?  It's not safe up there.  Come down."  You point out that if you could come down on your own you would have.  Alice wanders off muttering something under her breath.  You think it has something to do with brownies, but maybe you're just being paranoid.  You hear something clattering through the door and finally Alice arrives with a ladder.  She puts it where the stairs used to be and you are free to come down from the tower if you like.  Alice's expression says she highly recommends it.\par
\cf1 \par
down\par
\cf2 You move down.\par
You are below the bell tower.  They will probably repair the stairway soon.  Also here is a ladder.  You can move east and up.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
The sanctuary has a high arched roof.  A few of the stained glass windows have been broken, but most are still intact.  They are mostly light blue and depict religious scenes, chalices and lillies.  Above the door is the impressive rose window which has images of Matthew, Mark, Luke and John.  At the northern end of the sanctuary is the area that once held the altar.  The attractiveness of the room is marred somewhat by the presence of a large pile of garbage in the corner.   To the west is the bell tower.   Alice and Facha are here.  You can move south, west and out.\par
\cf1 \par
put shovel under garbage\par
\cf2 The shovel is under the pile of garbage.\par
\cf1 \par
put rake on garbage\par
\cf2 The rake is on top of the pile of garbage.\par
\cf1 \par
take garbage\par
\cf2 Congratulations.  You have picked up the half a ton of garbage.   In a balancing act that would impress the flying Walendas, you manage to get the half a ton of garbage out of the church only to discover that it is far to bulky to fit in your red VW microbus.  You are left standing outside the church, scratching your head, trying to figure out how to make it fit.  You are in front of a gothic wooden church.  The paint is peeling and the stained glass windows are in disrepair, but it retains much of its beauty and charm especially at this time of year.   Although the colors reached their peak a couple of weeks ago there are still enough orange leaves on the trees to remind you of a New England post card.  On the east side of the church you can make out Alice's garden.  Your VW microbus is parked here on a road heading north.  You'll have to get back in the bus if you want to go that way.  It's too far to walk.  There is a mailbox here.  You can move north and east.\par
\cf1 \par
break garbage with implement of destruction\par
\cf2 The garbage is now mashed, crushed, smashed and compacted to a much more manageable size.\par
\cf1 \par
break garbage\par
\cf2 With what do you wish to do that?\par
\cf1 \par
mash garbage\par
\cf2 You have already done that.\par
\cf1 \par
get out of bus\par
\cf2 You are no longer in the bus.\par
\cf1 \par
get out of bus\par
\cf2 You are no longer in the bus.\par
\cf1 \par
look\par
\cf2 You are in front of a gothic wooden church.  The paint is peeling and the stained glass windows are in disrepair, but it retains much of its beauty and charm especially at this time of year.   Although the colors reached their peak a couple of weeks ago there are still enough orange leaves on the trees to remind you of a New England post card.  On the east side of the church you can make out Alice's garden.  Your VW microbus is parked here on a road heading north.  You'll have to get back in the bus if you want to go that way.  It's too far to walk.  There is a mailbox here.  You can move north and east.\par
